ych as Kin, I Do, Do I? and Emerald Hill - The Little Nyonya Story.","title":"Ferlyn Wong","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferlyn_Wong"}},"Q21059878":{"id":"Q21059878","name":"Lee Mi-joo","ko":"이미주","birthName":"이미주","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Mijoo","Lee Seung-a"],"birth":"1994-09-23","death":"","birthplace":"Okcheon County","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2014","agencies":[{"name":"Woollim Entertainment","id":"Q50596","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Antenna","id":"Q4771243","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q18437003","name":"Lovelyz","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/queen.chu_s/","x":"https://x.com/LeeMiJoo","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/bb385616-64eb-462b-a80e-abd7763c0f17"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Seung-ah, known as Mijoo (미주), is a South Korean singer and entertainer. She debuted as a member of South Korean girl group Lovelyz under Woollim Entertainment in November 2014. Apart from her group's activities, Mijoo has starred in various Korean variety shows such as, Hit The Stage (2016), Dunia: Into a New World (2018), Sixth Sense (2020–2022), Hangout with Yoo (2021) and season 2 of Learn Way (2021–2022). Mijoo made her acting debut with I'm a Job Seeker (2016). On November 16, 2021, she left Woollim Entertainment after deciding not to renew her contract, and later joined Antenna. Mijoo made her solo debut with the single album Movie Star on May 17, 2023.","title":"Mijoo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mijoo"}},"Q21060390":{"id":"Q21060390","name":"Cha Eun-woo","ko":"차은우","birthName":"이동민","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Dong-min"],"birth":"1997-03-30","death":"","birthplace":"Gunpo","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","dancer","presenter","model"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"Fantagio","id":"Q13424955","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q23004252","name":"Astro","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/eunwo.o_c/","x":"https://x.com/CHAEUNWOO_offcl","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC3917z86gdSnaQ59L6Cj05w","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@at_chaeunwoo","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/7052bd1f-539d-4f61-80eb-c77a2b7cb38d"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Dong-min, known professionally as Cha Eun-woo, is a South Korean singer and actor. He is a member of the South Korean boy band Astro, and debuted as a solo artist with the extended play (EP) Entity in 2024. Cha made his acting debut in the film My Brilliant Life (2014) and gained widespread recognition through his lead roles in television series such as Gangnam Beauty (2018), Rookie Historian Goo Hae-ryung (2019), and True Beauty (2020–2021), the latter contributing to his international recognition as a figure of the Korean Wave. He has since starred in Island (2022–2023), A Good Day to Be a Dog (2023–2024), and Wonderful World (2024), and the film The First Ride (2025).","title":"Cha Eun-woo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cha_Eun-woo"}},"Q21577062":{"id":"Q21577062","name":"Yubin","ko":"유빈","birthName":"배유빈","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Bae Yubin","Bae Yoo-bin","Binnie"],"birth":"1997-09-09","death":"","birthplace":"Chuncheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[{"name":"WM Entertainment","id":"Q19794482","start":"","end":""},{"name":"DSP Media","id":"Q489428","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q19794854","name":"Oh My Girl","start":"2015","end":""},{"id":"Q65054131","name":"Oh My Girl Banhana","start":"2018","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/baeyu_b/","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1vpf88lk0FxD1ir2rbEryY","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/01e04a31-2688-4c00-ad18-a63ad46ce005"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Oh My Girl is a South Korean girl group formed by WM Entertainment and is currently under DSP Media. The group is composed of six members: Hyojung, Mimi, YooA, Seunghee, Yubin and Arin. Oh My Girl was originally an eight-piece group; JinE left the group in October 2017 due to health issues, and Jiho left in May 2022. Oh My Girl debuted on April 20, 2015, with an eponymous extended play.","title":"Binnie (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binnie_%28singer%29"}},"Q233894":{"id":"Q233894","name":"Sunny","ko":"써니","birthName":"Susan Soonkyu Lee","birthNameEn":"Susan Soonkyu Lee","aliases":["Lee Soon-kyu","Susan Soonkyu Lee"],"birth":"1989-05-15","death":"","birthplace":"Orange","nationality":["United States","South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","dancer","radio personality","composer","model"],"debut":"2007","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q20153","name":"Girls' Generation","start":"2007","end":""},{"id":"Q56260975","name":"Girls' Generation-Oh!GG","start":"2018","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/515sunnyday/","x":"https://x.com/515sunnyday","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/3c59eca2-15d4-425f-8b5d-043470c83635"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Susan Soonkyu Lee, known professionally as Sunny, is a South Korean and American singer and entertainer based in South Korea. She debuted as a member of girl group Girls' Generation (and later its subgroup Girls' Generation-Oh!GG) in August 2007, which went on to become one of the best-selling artists in South Korea and one of South Korea's most widely known girl groups worldwide. Apart from her group's activities, Sunny has participated in numerous side projects including original soundtracks, television variety shows, musical acting and radio hosting.","title":"Sunny (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunny_%28singer%29"}},"Q3457830":{"id":"Q3457830","name":"Wang Feifei","ko":"페이","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Fei"],"birth":"1987-04-27","death":"","birthplace":"Haikou","nationality":["People's Republic 